language-UndergroundCodespeak-name = Underground Codespeak
chat-language-UndergroundCodespeak-name = Underground Codespeak
language-UndergroundCodespeak-description = 
    Living a criminal life under the Trans-Solarian Federation in the Perseus Arm was a dangerous gambit.
    To avoid being caught saying something incriminating in the TSF's surveillance state and almost certainly executed by firing squad, crime families resorted to euphemisms.
    A long cat-and-mouse game between TSF authorities and the crime families has led to these euphemisms becoming multi-faceted, arguably nonsensical and far too detached from their origins to infer their meanings, while still designed to sound natural to a surveillance centre barely paying attention.
    Due to its extremely overcomplicated nature, most modern criminals opt to use translator implants rather than attempt to memorise the entire system manually.

